  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「カミヤツデ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AB%E3%83%9F%E3%83%A4%E3%83%84%E3%83%87",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106353289,
      "text": "カミヤツデ とはウコギ科の常緑低木。別名、ツウソウ（通草）、 ツウダツボク（通脱木）。カミヤツデ属唯一の現生種である。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Tetrapanax」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetrapanax",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1354642362,
      "text": "Tetrapanax papyrifer, the rice paper plant, is an evergreen shrub or small tree in the family Araliaceae, the sole species in the genus Tetrapanax. The specific epithet is frequently misspelled as \"papyriferum\", \"papyriferus\", or \"papyrifera\". It is native to eastern and central China and Taiwan, but widely cultivated in East Asia and in other tropical to mild temperate regions as well."
    }
